course: dictionary
lesson: 946
title: Blonde: hair, colour and people
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Blonde is a word you will meet in stories and in real life. As an adjective it means having pale yellow or golden hair, or being pale yellow or golden in colour, like light hair, wood or beer. You can use the context to check: «A head has about 100,000 hairs; blondes often have more and redheads fewer.» The words about hairs show that blonde is describing hair.
explain: Swap your meaning into the sentence to test it. Does "blondes often have more hairs" still make sense if blonde means pale golden hair? Yes, so your meaning fits.
explain: Blonde can also be a noun: a blonde is a person with blonde hair. This is mostly used for women, and it can sound rude. Remember that blonde is a colour word, so it describes hair. It does not tell you anything about how clever a person is.
explain: Other languages have hair colour words too. In French, «brun» or «brune» means dark-haired, «blond» or «blonde» means blond, and «roux» or «rousse» means ginger. «Cheveux rouges» would mean hair dyed bright red.
fact: Blonde means having pale yellow or golden hair.
fact: Blonde can also describe colours like wood or beer, which are pale yellow or golden.
fact: A blonde is a noun for a person with blonde hair, and it is mostly used for women; it can sound rude.
fact: «Blonde jokes» that say blonde people are not clever are an unkind stereotype, and they are not true.
fact: A head has about 100,000 hairs, and losing about 50 to 100 hairs a day is normal.
exercise: In French, «brun» means dark-haired. What does «blond» mean? | Ginger | *Blond | Bright red | Dark-haired
exercise: Which word means pale yellow or golden, like light hair, wood or beer? | Straight | Dark-haired | *Blonde | Ginger
exercise: Which thing does blonde describe in «blondes often have more and redheads fewer»? | Weather | Houses | *Hair | Shoes
test: Which French word means ginger hair? | brune | blond | *roux | brun
test: Which statement is true? | *Blonde is a hair colour, and it says nothing about how clever someone is | Blonde people are not clever | Blonde jokes are a fair way to laugh at people | Blonde means dark
exam: In «blondes often have more hairs», what does blondes mean? | *People with blonde hair | Dark-haired people | Hair dye | Long hair
